      "title": "Troubleshooting Data Pipeline Export Corruption and Encoding Mismatches",
      "content_summary": "This article addresses common symptoms like garbled characters, missing records, and corrupted exports in Data Pipeline jobs, outlining the typical causes related to migration defects and schema mismatches.",
      "content_body": "When users report garbled characters or missing data in exports, first verify that the source and target schemas are aligned and that encoding settings match. These issues often stem from incomplete migrations or data quality problems introduced during transfer. If records are missing, check for data truncation errors in the job logs. Resolutions typically involve running a data repair script to fix malformed entries or performing a full data re-sync to restore synchronization. In cases of severe schema drift, a controlled schema migration may be required before re-attempting the pipeline execution."
